WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.689
For this practice we change the fixed reference date
Instead of August

00:00:05.715 --> 00:00:11.387
eleventh use August fifth twenty twenty-six Before
running the query predict

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.549
which admissions will move outside the thirty-day
window This is a good

00:00:15.575 --> 00:00:20.459
exercise because it separates two different parts of
the logic Changing the

00:00:20.485 --> 00:00:24.879
reference date changes which records are included in
the cohort It does

00:00:24.905 --> 00:00:28.191
not change the rule that uses diagnosis and age to
assign the

00:00:28.204 --> 00:00:33.294
risk category If you want copy the earlier date
query into pgAdmin

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.173
and change only the reference date You can also make
the same

00:00:37.199 --> 00:00:40.974
change in the browser code Try to change one part of
the

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.072
rule at a time That makes it much easier to
understand why

00:00:45.098 --> 00:00:46.206
the output changes
